From lens formula
$\begin{array}{l}
\frac{1}{f}=\left(a \mu_g-1\right)\left(\frac{1}{R_1}-\frac{1}{R_2}\right) \\
=\because(1.5-1)\left(\frac{1}{R_1}-\frac{1}{R_2}\right)...(i)
\end{array}
Also, $\mu_g=\frac{\mu_g}{\mu_l}=\frac{1.5}{1.6}\begin{aligned}
& \therefore \frac{1}{f^{\prime}} =\left(, \mu_g-1\right)\left(\frac{1}{R_1}-\frac{1}{R_2}\right) \\
& \frac{1}{f^{\prime}} =\left(\frac{15}{16}-1\right)\left(\frac{1}{R_1}-\frac{1}{R_2}\right)....(ii)
\end{aligned}$
Dividing Eq. (i) by Eq. (ii), we get
$\begin{aligned}
\frac{f}{f^{\prime}} & =\frac{\left(\frac{15}{16}-1\right)}{(1.5-1)}=-\frac{1}{16 \times 5} \\
\Rightarrow f & =-160 \mathrm{~cm}
\end{aligned}

